  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Arun Kumar Gantayat vs State Of Odisha .... Opposite Party on 15 September, 2023 Author: V. Narasingh Bench: V. Narasingh In The High Court Of Orissa At Cuttack Blapl No.9375 of 2023 Arun Kumar Gantayat .... Petitioner Mr. P. Das, Advocate -versus- State of Odisha .... Opposite Party Mr. H.K. Panigrahi, Asc Coram: Justice V. Narasingh Order 15.09.2023 Order No. 02. 1.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2. The Petitioner is an accused in G.R. Case No.527 of 2023 pending on the file of learned J.M.F.C-III (Cog. Taking), Cuttack, arising out of Malgodown P.S. Case No.143 of 2023 for commission of the alleged offence under Sections 420/272/273 IPC and Sections 51/52/59/63/57 of the Food Safety and Stand Act and Section 14 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. 4. It is submitted by the learned counsel that the Petitioner is in custody since 22.7.2023 and the allegation against him is that he is actively involved in adulterating the spices by adding chemical colour etc. which are not fit for human consumption. 5. Learned counsel for the State opposes the prayer for bail during currency of investigation. 6. Learned counsel for the Petitioner submits that the Petitioner is the first offender.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2. The Petitioner is an accused in G.R. Case No.527 of 2023 pending on the file of learned J.M.F.C-III (Cog. Taking), Cuttack, arising out of Malgodown P.S. Case No.143 of 2023 for commission of the alleged offence under Sections 420/272/273 IPC and Sections 51/52/59/63/57 of the Food Safety and Stand Act and Section 14 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act. 4. It is submitted by the learned counsel that the Petitioner is in custody since 22.7.2023 and the allegation against him is that he is actively involved in adulterating the spices by adding chemical colour etc. which are not fit for human consumption. 5. Learned counsel for the State opposes the prayer for bail during currency of investigation.",
    "respondent_arguments": "6. Learned counsel for the Petitioner submits that the Petitioner is the first offender.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
